-- title:
--   Valuation rings at a supersingular point pinned by floor residues
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, a characteristic-zero field $L$ that is a $p$-th cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and $K_1 \le K$ the one generated by the $q$-expansion field of $\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal, $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and maximal ideal generated by $\varpi$, acting on $K$ and $K_1$ compatibly with $L$; let $j \in K$ and $j_1 \in K_1$ be nonzero elements whose Laurent series is the image of the $q$-expansion of $j$. Let $W_0$ be the valuation subring of $K$ consisting of those $f$ for which there are power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal and $f \cdot y = x$ in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$, and assume $W_0$ contains the chart algebra $\mathtt{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$. Let $y$ be a point of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of this chart algebra whose prime ideal contains the image of $\varpi$, such that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in $\mathtt{ssJSet}\,p\,\Omega$, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $p$-torsion point; assume moreover some element of the prime ideal of $y$ is a unit of $W_0$. Call a valuation subring $P$ of the residue field of $W_0$ admissible if it contains the residues of all chart-algebra elements and if a chart element's residue is a nonunit of $P$ exactly when the element lies in the prime ideal of $y$. The conclusion asserts two things: first, an arbitrary valuation subring $P'$ of the residue field of $W_0$ that contains exactly the same residues of elements $u \in K_1$ whose image in $K$ lies in $W_0$ as an admissible $P$ does must equal $P$; second, for every admissible $P$ and every $e \in P$ there is such a $u \in K_1$ with $e$ minus the residue of $u$ a nonunit of $P$.
--
--   This is Igusa's total ramification of the Igusa curve over the supersingular points of $X_1(M)$, transported to the residue field of the Gauss valuation ring on the stable model of $X_1(Mp)$: at a supersingular point not the centre of the Gauss ring, a valuation subring centred there is determined by, and generated modulo its maximal ideal by, the residues of the elements of the level-$\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p)$ subfield. It is used by [`ModularCurve.XOneP.comap_eq_of_forall_apply_eq_of_map_jChartFin_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.comap_eq_of_forall_apply_eq_of_map_jChartFin_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel_x1_mul) and [`ModularCurve.XOneP.forall_smul_sub_mem_of_smul_eq_of_map_jChartFin_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.forall_smul_sub_mem_of_smul_eq_of_map_jChartFin_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel_x1_mul), which identify stabilisers and displacements of chart automorphisms at supersingular points.
